The error is `REQUIRED_FIELD_MISSING: [Name]` on the Account insert. Even though NPSP auto-generates the household name, the `Name` field is required at the database level, so DML will reject an Account insert with no Name at all.

**Fix:** Set a placeholder `Name` (the first contact's `LastName`) so the DML passes. Then, when we update `npe01__One2OneContact__c`, NPSP's Household Naming trigger/automation fires and **overwrites** the placeholder with the real generated household name (e.g. "The Smith Family"). We never compute the household name ourselves — we only seed a required-field value.

